# A DHCPDISCOVER as it arrived on the wire: one Ethernet frame, 342
# bytes, exactly as captured.
#
# Observed on 2026-11-21 at Unix time 1795245117.944749, on the bridge
# br-n1 of the Linux-bridge lab -- ISC dhclient on a client endpoint,
# Debian 13, kernel 6.12.117+deb13-amd64. The exchange this frame opens
# is answered by response.hex. case.toml beside this file carries the
# capture's full provenance and the docs/provenance.md rows the pair
# supports.
#
# These are bytes observed coming out of a running program. Nothing here
# is derived from anybody's source code, and nothing may be.
#
# Hex text rather than a binary blob, for two reasons: a reviewer can
# read the diff when a fixture changes, and the bytes can carry the
# field annotations below. The harness strips comments and whitespace
# and compares what decodes. The annotations are a reading aid; the
# bytes are what the rig asserts on.

